essbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKENOUCHI, OSAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANI, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Novel compounds exhibiting chymase-inhibiting activities and being useful as various drugs, i.e., SF2809-I, SF2809-II, SF2809-III, SF2809-IV, SF2809-V and SF2809-VI substances represented by general formula (VII), and pharmaceutically acceptable salts thereof: [wherein R&lt;1&gt; is hydrogen, phenyl or p-hydroxyphenyl; and R&lt;2&gt; is acetylamino(-NHCOCH3) or hydroxyl]; a process for the preparation of SF2809 substances; and drug compositions containing the same.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne de nouveaux composés présentant un activité d'inhibition de la chymase, et utiles en tant que médicaments divers, par exemple les substances SF2809-I, SF2809-II, SF2809-III, SF2809-IV, SF2809-V, et SF2809-VI représentées par la formule générale (VII), ainsi que les sels pharmaceutiquement acceptables de ces composés. Dans la formule précitée, R&lt;1&gt; représente hydrogène, phényle ou p-hydroxyphényle ; et R&lt;2&gt; représente acétylamino(-NHCOCH3) ou hydroxyle. L'invention concerne également un procédé de préparation des substances 2809, ainsi que des compositions de médicaments renfermant lesdites substances.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence